{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024","id":4956525987,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJgfwyc8AAAABJ26Vow","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024","diff_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pull/1024.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/1024/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/issues/1024/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/statuses/2cc562fa39f7b430c61a4494636f6ee0ec0d631a","number":1024,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix: retain bounded terminal cloud diagnostics","user":{"login":"tangtaoit","id":3895878,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTU4Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3895878?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit","html_url":"https://github.com/tangtaoit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tangtaoit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Terminal cloud diagnostics could omit the workload’s already-produced failure examples and lose the entire Prometheus range when a response exceeded 4 MiB. The range also followed collection time instead of the terminal report. This change retains bounded, validated worker/status documents and eight fixed metric partitions anchored to that report, preserving successful partitions and explicitly recording missing or partial evidence.\n\nThe collector binds run/generation/snapshot identity, retains raw timestamp precision while using Prometheus millisecond query bounds, and requires a valid failed-before-capacity state before exempting missing capacity documents. The metric partitions share 24 MiB and 60 seconds. Product runtime, zero-loss qualification and cloud lifecycle are unchanged.\n\nValidation includes tests-first implementation, 79 real collector process cases across 20 Python methods, two Go integration entrypoints, and independent Standards/Spec reviews. The initial millisecond-boundary and capacity-state findings were fixed and independently rechecked. Full scripts default tests and the supplementary Mac integration suite passed; the latter used a documented 12-minute local watchdog and does not replace Linux policy.\n\nThe first Linux candidate run [39654237841](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39654237841) passed default tests and migration/messaging E2E, but scripts reached the original 600-second outer limit before completing all cases. No assertion failure was observed; this remains a failed gate. The first [three-node performance/correctness run](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39654237861) passed separately. All first-run evidence is retained.\n\nA test-only follow-up prepares synthetic SSH response files once per case instead of repeatedly starting Python. It preserves the real collector process boundary, all 20 test-method bodies, every one of the 79 scenarios, and the original test concurrency and deadlines. The first focused follow-up passed both Go entries (retention: 60.60 seconds locally). All 79 complete receipts match the original behavior, with only capture wall-clock timestamps normalized after validating the original file hashes. The next head still needs its first full Linux policy check before merge; local timing is not proof that the 600-second gate has recovered.\n\nThe original cloud message-loss cause remains unproven. This PR repairs diagnostic retention and does not claim to repair or waive that verdict. No new cloud run or release is started by this change.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T18:36:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T19:11:07Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"45c1f5da10721c9be1c9907be098a11118a92f0f","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"WuKongIM:codex/v3-rc-terminal-evidence","ref":"codex/v3-rc-terminal-evidence","repo":{"id":638054601,"node_id":"R_kgDOJgfwyQ","name":"WuKongIM","full_name":"WuKongIM/WuKongIM","owner":{"login":"WuKongIM","id":132860831,"node_id":"O_kgDOB-tLnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132860831?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM","html_url":"https://github.com/WuKongIM","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WuKongIM/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"descripti